                <pb facs="0719" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg705"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Commandant Newton,
                        United States Navy, to Lieutenant-Commander Totten, United States Navy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Sealed orders.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><date calendar="gregorian" when="1849-08-20"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >August</hi> 20, 1849</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: You will proceed direct with the United
                    States steamer Water Witch, under your command, to Cat Island, and there join
                    the United States ship Albany, Commodore V. M. Randolph, and assist him in
                    carrying out the instructions of the honorable Secretary of the Navy, a copy of
                    which accompanies this.</p>
                <p>Should you not fall in with the Albany at Cat Island, or its vicinity, you will
                    proceed to Balize, in further pursuance of the orders.</p>
                <p>Wishing you a pleasant cruise, I am, very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>JOHN THOMAS NEWTON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Commandant.</hi></item>
                            <item>Lieutenant-Commander <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. M.
                                    Totten</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States Steamer
                                    Water Witch.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
